{"title":"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131f50fd2ca9d36154bd969bc4405c7648ce3e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{x} \\cdot 10^{5} = 100^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26474152698e49d126b2230b7123b166c62b78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   1 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   35 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   11 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   \\frac{4}{5} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   3 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"406\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using exponent rules, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131f50fd2ca9d36154bd969bc4405c7648ce3e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{x} \\cdot 10^{5} = 100^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee25b3014e9de744e1381cd2b4ac0c6b5bc208a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{x + 5} = (10^{2})^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7a2e00009cd13d850234019000b3c9886c1592.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{x + 5} = 10^{2 \\times 4} = 10^{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Since the bases are equal and aren't <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can equate the exponents:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5ab1ac4a84c8ea37ce646b3435b1d5df58ac8ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 5 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b809ffb660fea28acfea3426a44c2e080af74d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 8 - 5 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"155\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat\">2014 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html